@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 Kafka consumer: poll pack, Actor callback, retry, timeout and commit
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #253746
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #334155
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #111827
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF5CC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #8A5A00
skinparam NoteFontColor #111827
skinparam GroupBorderColor #176B87
skinparam GroupBackgroundColor #EEF6F8
skinparam GroupFontColor #111827

participant "Partition Manager" as Part
participant "RE Consumer Thread" as Loop
participant "Abstract Consumer Template" as Abstract
participant "KafkaConsumer" as Kafka
participant "Submit Strategy" as Submit
participant "Pack Context" as Pack
participant "App / Tenant / RuleChain / Node Actors" as Actor
participant "Async DB / External Node" as External
participant "Processing Strategy" as Strategy
participant "Kafka Group Coordinator" as Group

== Subscription is applied by poll ==
Part -> Abstract: subscribe(Set<TopicPartitionInfo>)
activate Abstract
Abstract -> Abstract: subscribeQueue.add(latest topics)
Abstract --> Part: return before Kafka subscribe
deactivate Abstract

Loop -> Abstract: poll(queue.pollInterval)
activate Abstract
Abstract -> Abstract: lock consumerLock
Abstract -> Abstract: drain subscribeQueue and keep latest set
Abstract -> Kafka: subscribe(full topic names)
Kafka -> Group: join or update consumer group
Group --> Kafka: assignment after poll protocol
Abstract -> Kafka: poll(Duration)
Kafka -> Kafka: local positions advance for returned records
Kafka --> Abstract: ConsumerRecords<String, byte[]>
Abstract -> Abstract: decode every record to Protobuf queue message
Abstract --> Loop: decoded pack
deactivate Abstract

== First processing attempt ==
Loop -> Submit: new strategy then init(pack)
Loop -> Strategy: new processing strategy
Loop -> Pack: new context(pending map, latch)
Loop -> Submit: submitAttempt(callback factory)
loop according to BURST / BATCH / sequential mode
  Submit -> Loop: submitMessage(id, proto)
  Loop -> Actor: ActorSystemContext.tell(QueueToRuleEngineMsg)
end
Loop -> Pack: await(packProcessingTimeout)
activate Pack

par message A succeeds
  Actor -> External: database or external side effect
  External --> Actor: async completion
  Actor -> Pack: TbMsgPackCallback.onSuccess(idA)
  Pack -> Pack: pending to success and decrement
  Pack -> Submit: onSuccess(idA) may release next sequential msg
else message B fails
  Actor -> Pack: onFailure(idB, error)
  Pack -> Pack: pending to failed and decrement
else message C remains pending
  Actor -> External: slow asynchronous work
end

alt all callbacks before timeout
  Pack --> Loop: latch completed
else timeout
  Pack --> Loop: await false with pending messages
end
deactivate Pack

Loop -> Strategy: analyze(success, failed, pending)
activate Strategy
alt SKIP strategy or retry limit reached
  Strategy --> Loop: decision commit=true
else RETRY strategy
  Strategy -> Strategy: select configured result maps
  opt pauseBetweenRetries
    Strategy -> Strategy: sleep in consumer thread
  end
  Strategy --> Loop: decision commit=false plus reprocess map
end
deactivate Strategy
Loop -> Pack: cleanup and clear maps

alt decision requests retry
  Loop -> Submit: update(reprocess map)
  Loop -> Pack: create new context and callbacks
  Loop -> Actor: resubmit selected in-memory messages
  note over Actor,External
    Effects from the previous attempt are not rolled back.
    Old asynchronous work may overlap the retry attempt.
  end note
else decision commits
  Loop -> Submit: stop()
  Loop -> Abstract: commit()
  Abstract -> Kafka: commitSync()
  Kafka -> Group: commit current assignment positions
  Group --> Kafka: commit result
  Abstract --> Loop: commit completed
end

== Late callback after timeout cleanup ==
External --> Actor: old attempt completes
Actor -> Pack: callback checks isMsgValid()
alt strategy can skip timed-out callbacks
  Pack --> Actor: false, stop continuation
else Main SKIP_ALL_FAILURES compatibility path
  Pack --> Actor: true, chain may continue
  Actor -> Pack: success/failure finds cleared pending map
end

== Decode poison boundary ==
Loop -> Abstract: next poll()
Abstract -> Kafka: poll()
Kafka --> Abstract: records and advanced local position
Abstract -> Abstract: decoder throws IOException
Abstract --> Loop: RuntimeException
Loop -> Loop: catch, log, sleep
note over Abstract,Group
  No seek is issued. A later successful commit may advance
  the group offset beyond this undecoded record.
end note

== Long retry and rebalance ==
Loop -> Loop: await or retry longer than max.poll.interval
Group -> Kafka: revoke assignment / rebalance
Group -> Kafka: another member receives uncommitted records
Loop -> Abstract: commit after processing
Abstract -> Kafka: commitSync()
Kafka --> Abstract: CommitFailed or rebalance exception
Abstract --> Loop: exception, outer loop logs and continues

== Partition removal and close ==
Part -> Loop: initiateStop removed consumer task
Loop -> Loop: exit after current control point
Loop -> Abstract: unsubscribe()
Abstract -> Kafka: unsubscribe then close
Kafka -> Group: leave group
@enduml
